<p data-v-039ffd48="" class="para">NVIDIA GeForce® NOW™ turns your LG TV into a powerful gaming PC.<br> <br> Users can stream games from their library or purchase new titles from popular digital stores like Steam, Epic Games Store, Ubisoft Connect, and Origin. Access over 800 games, with new titles added every Thursday. The service boasts a catalog of popular games, including over 35 free-to-play titles like Fortnite, Apex Legends, and Destiny 2. Play with millions of other players in 1080p at 60 FPS, without downloading, installing, or waiting for updates or patches.<br> <br> A subscription is required to play GeForce NOW. Try cloud gaming on your PC with our free subscription. Looking for more? Subscribe to Premium and get priority access to game servers, longer sessions, high FPS and RTX technologies in supported games. Detailed information on registration in GeForce NOW and subscription options can be found at https://gfn.ru/.<br> <br> Don't have an account in any digital store yet? After subscribing to GeForce NOW, you can create an account in Steam, Epic Games Store, Ubisoft Connect or Origin.<br> <br> To play, you need to use a gamepad, such as an Xbox, PlayStation or NVIDIA SHIELD controller. A full list of supported gamepads can be found here: geforcenow.com/requirements.<br> <br> For the best gaming experience, we recommend connecting your LG TV to the internet via an Ethernet cable or 5 GHz WiFi.<br> <br>GeForce NOW for 2022 LG TVs is currently in beta mode and is available on select 2021, 2022 LG TVs.<br><br>A list of compatible LG TVs can be found here: https://nvda.ws/383TCVd<br></p>